Discovery policies added after deployment.

The agent takes a single agent.yaml. `diode-agent policy add <file>` merges a
policy file from this directory into the rendered /etc/diode/agent/agent.yaml
and restarts the agent; `diode-agent policy test <file>` runs it once and
prints what it would ingest without sending anything.

Each file here is the `policies:` fragment for one backend, for example:

    device_discovery:
      core_switches:
        config:
          schedule: "0 2 * * *"
        scope:
          - hostname: 192.0.2.10
            username: ${SWITCH_USERNAME}
            password: ${SWITCH_PASSWORD}
            driver: ios

Credentials are ${VARIABLE} references, resolved from
/etc/diode/agent/credentials.env (mode 0600). Do not write a secret into a
file in this directory: it is captured by diode-backup and shown by
diode-support-bundle.

Backends: network_discovery (nmap sweeps), device_discovery (driver-based
polling), snmp_discovery, gnmi_discovery, worker. See the orb-agent
documentation for each backend's policy schema.
